WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.859
Sense compares reality with
the written prediction.

00:00:02.929 --> 00:00:08.177
The first reading occurs after the thin slice
and asks whether the critical assumption holds.

00:00:08.247 --> 00:00:12.855
Use the metric definition and
thresholds agreed before the experiment.

00:00:12.925 --> 00:00:15.826
Include failures, exclusions, and exceptions.

00:00:15.896 --> 00:00:20.867
An improvement on a selected subset may
disappear when failed tasks are restored.

00:00:20.937 --> 00:00:26.078
Write the result in a delta log: predicted,
observed, model update, and decision.

00:00:26.148 --> 00:00:31.119
The twelve-task assisted sample has a
median of 12 minutes and one wrong queue.

00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:34.111
It meets the fictional speed
and quality thresholds.

00:00:34.181 --> 00:00:39.579
Two additional unusable tickets were rejected
before review and must be reported as

00:00:39.649 --> 00:00:40.843
exclusions.

00:00:40.913 --> 00:00:45.692
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

00:00:45.762 --> 00:00:50.690
Write a delta entry that includes the
sample denominator and excluded records.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.133
Predicted: median no greater than
14 with at most one misroute.

00:00:55.203 --> 00:01:01.710
Observed: median 12, one misroute across twelve
eligible tasks, plus two rejected inputs.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:06.047
Update: routing assistance is
promising within eligible tasks.

00:01:06.117 --> 00:01:10.597
Decision: prepare a controlled landing
only after checklist gaps close.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:14.549
Do not generalize this synthetic
result to all support work.

00:01:14.619 --> 00:01:17.222
What should the report do with rejected inputs?

00:01:17.292 --> 00:01:18.572
A. Hide them B.

00:01:18.642 --> 00:01:21.095
Include them as successful reviews C.

00:01:21.165 --> 00:01:23.661
Report their count and exclusion reason.

00:01:23.731 --> 00:01:25.139
The best answer is C.

00:01:25.209 --> 00:01:28.196
Coverage and exclusions affect interpretation.
